@startuml
' Class structure of the WebGIS client: the component only knows the MapService,
' which keeps the two interchangeable map engines behind one interface.
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Inter
skinparam roundCorner 8
skinparam classFontColor black
skinparam classAttributeFontColor black

skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor<<ui>> #FFF3E0
  BorderColor<<ui>> #F57C00
  BackgroundColor<<facade>> #E3F2FD
  BorderColor<<facade>> #1976D2
  BackgroundColor<<engine>> #E0F2F1
  BorderColor<<engine>> #00897B
  BackgroundColor<<service>> #F3E5F5
  BorderColor<<service>> #7B1FA2
}

class App <<ui>> {
  Signals: cities, selectedGenera, route …
  --
  selectCity(), toggleGenus()
  setMapEngine(kind)
  computeRoute()
}

class MapService <<facade>> {
  engineKind: Signal<EngineKind>
  gpuCaveat, slowFrameMs
  --
  createMap(target, popup, callbacks)
  switchEngine(kind)
  .. remembered for the replay ..
  filter · visibility · route · markers
}

interface MapEngine <<engine>> {
  create(target, popup, cb, view)
  destroy() : void
  viewState() : ViewState
  setFilter(genera, cityId)
  drawRoute(coords)
  hidePopup()
}

class OlEngine <<engine>> {
  OpenLayers + WMS images
  filter → CQL to the server
  GetFeatureInfo for popups
}

class MaplibreEngine <<engine>> {
  MapLibre GL + vector tiles
  filter → style filter on the GPU
  zoom ladder: city points →
  grid cells → individual trees
  measures frame times (auto hint)
}

class RoutingService <<service>> {
  route(): tube, convergence,
  crossings, direct route, cache
}
class GeoServerService <<service>> {
  WFS statistics, CQL building
}
class CatalogService <<service>> {
  city list (alphabetical)
}
class GeocoderService <<service>> {
  address search, online fallback
}
class StatusService <<service>> {
  loading status per module
}

App --> MapService : the only\ndoor
App --> RoutingService
App --> GeoServerService
App --> CatalogService
App --> GeocoderService
App --> StatusService

MapService o--> "1" MapEngine : active engine\n(lazily loaded)
MapEngine <|.. OlEngine
MapEngine <|.. MaplibreEngine

note right of MapService
  On switching: take the camera from the
  old engine, tear it down, load the new
  one — then replay filter, visibility,
  route and markers.
end note

note bottom of MapEngine
  The contract of both views.
  A new engine only has to fulfil
  these methods; app and services
  stay untouched.
end note
@enduml
